    "body": "Second Windows 11 check (Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26300, Intel UHD integrated, driver 32.0.101.7079, 16 GB, v0.23.0 zip):\n- No crash either: the UI started on dx12 (Intel UHD) and stayed up; `camcraft-cli process` exited 0 on all three examples.\n- **No CamCraft log file was found at all** under `%APPDATA%` or `%LOCALAPPDATA%` after two UI runs. So on Windows a user has nothing to send us. Point 1-3 of this issue are the fix.\n- Also seen: `camcraft-ui.exe <path>.camproj` ignores the path on the command line (the window opens \"Untitled\"). If the installer associates `.camproj`, a double-click in Explorer would open an empty project - worth checking in the same pass.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
