    "body": "Stopped after the required quick gate and a targeted gate retry failed the same unrelated motion test.\nThe failing test is a_narrow_second_piece_names_its_ramp_stand_in_at_each_level.\nIt expects a ramp note at (56, 5), but the notes name (56, 6).\nThe branch is stacked on #2110 at f69a955e5 because that PR changes the same GPU bring-up diagnostics.\nThat base predates #2427, merged as 70441839c, which fixes this motion failure on current upstream/main.\nI did not change machining code or update the parent branch.\n\nThe logging fix is held in .claude/worktrees/issue-2421 on issue/2421-startup-log.\nDesktop startup uses logging::init_desktop to append and synchronize GPU metadata, errors and panic backtraces to a platform log file.\nSynchronous append preserves the previous run without relying on shutdown flushes.\nCritical records bypass the verbosity filter and preserve the previous panic hook.\nCrash messages name the log path and backend retry flags.\nThe CLI keeps its stderr-only initializer so help stays quiet and avoids filesystem side effects.\nThis corrects the CLI regression found in the first gate.\n\nAll five new pins failed before the fix and pass now.\nThe latest CLI suite passes all 12 tests.\nGPU selection passes all 15 tests.\nDesktop wiring, panic-hook, logger and GPU metadata/hint mutations went red and returned green after restoration.\nThe latest touched-crate clippy passes with warnings denied.\nNo NC or CL goldens changed.\nWindows message boxes and physical GPU failures were not exercised.\n\nThe work remains uncommitted in that worktree.\nNo branch was pushed and no PR was opened because the required gate remains red.\nClaim released.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
